#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:10004
msgid "Using the Particles Class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:10006
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Gal3D` uses the {py:class}`Particles <gal3d.point.Particles>` class to "
"manage and operate on particle data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:20002
msgid ""
"To initialize the class, you need to provide particle positions (``pos``)"
" and masses (``mass``). Here we again use particle data from a galaxy in "
"TNG50-1 as an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:40002
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Use the {py:class}`Particles <gal3d.point.Particles>` class to initialize"
" particle positions and masses. The position array ``pos`` has shape "
"``(N, 3)``, and the mass array ``mass`` has shape ``(N,)``, where ``N`` "
"is the number of particles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:70002
msgid ""
"`recenter=False` keeps the original particle positions instead of "
"recentering them (the default is `True`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:70003
msgid ""
"`density_estimator` specifies the method used for density estimation. "
"Here we use `DensityEstimatorSPH`. You can call "
"`Particles.available_estimators` to see the list of available density "
"estimators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:90002
msgid "About Density Estimators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:90003
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When using `DensityEstimatorSPH`, density estimation is performed by "
"{py:class}`DensityEstimatorSPH "
"<gal3d.point.density_estimator_plugins.estimator_sph.DensityEstimatorSPH>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:90005
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{py:class}`DensityEstimatorSPH "
"<gal3d.point.density_estimator_plugins.estimator_sph.DensityEstimatorSPH>`"
" is a subclass of {py:class}`DensityEstimatorBase "
"<gal3d.point.density_estimator.DensityEstimatorBase>`. If you want to use"
" another density estimation method, you can define your own class by "
"inheriting from `DensityEstimatorBase`. Once such a custom estimator is "
"defined, it will be automatically registered in "
"`Particles.available_estimators`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:90007
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For more details on how `DensityEstimatorSPH` works, see {ref}`Density "
"Estimation <density-estimator>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:100002
msgid "Particle Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:100004
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{py:attr}`Particles.parameter <gal3d.point.Particles.parameter>`: the "
"density at each particle position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:100005
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{py:attr}`Particles.hsm <gal3d.point.Particles.hsm>`: the smoothing "
"length at each particle position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:120002
msgid "Querying the Density at Arbitrary Positions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:120004
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Use {py:meth}`Particles.get_parameter "
"<gal3d.point.Particles.get_parameter>` to query the density at any "
"coordinate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:140002
msgid "2D Density Projection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:140004
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"You can use {py:meth}`Particles.project_2d "
"<gal3d.point.Particles.project_2d>` to obtain a density projection of the"
" particles after smoothing with a kernel function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:160002
msgid ""
"Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) is widely used in fluid "
"simulations. By smoothing particle distributions, it can better capture "
"fine fluid structures. Below, we use gas particles as an example to show "
"their density distribution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:180005
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Gal3D` implements SPH projection using a two-step sampling and "
"renormalization scheme. A more detailed introduction and examples can be "
"found in {ref}`SPH Projection <SPH-render2d>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:190002
msgid "Obtaining the Shape at an Arbitrary Radius"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tutorials/particles.ipynb:190004
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"You can use {py:meth}`Particles.shape_at "
"<gal3d.point.Particles.shape_at>` to measure the shape at any radius. By "
"default, this method uses the ellipsoidal iterative shape estimator based"
" on the density field, namely {py:class}`EllipsoidalShapeEstimator "
"<gal3d.model_workflow.fit_workflow_plugins.iterate_ellipsoid_continuous.IterateEllipsoidDensity>`."
msgstr ""

